IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM syst.Guide WHERE Slug = 'foreign-scholarships-for-sri-lankan-students')
    INSERT INTO syst.Guide (Slug, CoverImageURL, Icon, Color, ContentJSON, SortOrder, IsActive)
    VALUES ('foreign-scholarships-for-sri-lankan-students', '', 'award', 'amber', N'{"en":{"title":"Foreign Scholarships for Sri Lankan Students 2027: Fully Funded Options Compared","seoTitle":"Foreign Scholarships for Sri Lankan Students 2027 | Proton","description":"Compare foreign scholarships for Sri Lankan students: China CSC, MEXT, GKS, Chevening and more, with coverage, windows and how to apply from Sri Lanka.","bodyHtml":"<p><strong>In short:</strong> Foreign scholarships for Sri Lankan students come from governments such as China, Japan, Korea, the UK, Australia, Germany, Türkiye, Hungary, Russia, India and Pakistan. Many are announced in Sri Lanka through the Ministry of Education, Higher Education and Vocational Education and the relevant embassy, and most are fully funded but highly competitive. Plan 9–12 months ahead, because most application windows open once a year.</p><p>This guide compares the main fully funded and partial scholarships open to Sri Lankans for 2026/2027 intakes, explains how each one is applied for from Sri Lanka, and gives a yearly calendar. Proton Education Services advises on China only, so the China options are covered in the most depth; for every other country, use the official links and always confirm the current call before you apply.</p><h2>How do Sri Lankan students apply for government scholarships abroad?</h2><p>Sri Lankan students apply for government-to-government scholarships in one of three ways: through a Ministry of Education nomination (often via the online portal at foreignscholarships.mohe.gov.lk), directly to the foreign embassy in Colombo, or directly online to the foreign government or university. Each scholarship states its own route in its call notice.</p><ul><li><strong>Ministry of Education nomination.</strong> The Ministry of Education, Higher Education and Vocational Education publishes scholarship notices on its website and screens Sri Lankan applicants before nominating them. Recent examples include the Japanese MEXT undergraduate scholarship for 2027 (online application only, through foreignscholarships.mohe.gov.lk), the Chinese Government Scholarship quota for Sri Lanka, Stipendium Hungaricum and the UK Commonwealth Scholarships. For some quotas the Ministry shortlists by A/L Z-score.</li><li><strong>Embassy route.</strong> Some programmes are run by the embassy itself. The Korean Embassy in Colombo, for example, has accepted Global Korea Scholarship (GKS) graduate applications by post or by hand at its Colombo 7 office, and the Japanese Embassy interviews MEXT candidates.</li><li><strong>Direct application.</strong> Chevening, Australia Awards, DAAD, Türkiye Burslari and university-level China scholarships take applications directly on their own websites.</li></ul><p>Some scholarships use two routes at once. Stipendium Hungaricum, for instance, needs an application on the Hungarian portal and a nomination from the home-country sending partner. Missing either step means rejection.</p><h2>Which foreign scholarships are open to Sri Lankans? (comparison table)</h2><p>The table below lists programmes where we could confirm Sri Lankan eligibility from an official or Sri Lankan source in October 2026. Application months are \"typical\" based on the most recent cycle found; they shift each year, so treat them as a planning guide, not a deadline.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Scholarship</th><th>Level</th><th>What it covers</th><th>Language requirement</th><th>Typical application window</th><th>How Sri Lankans apply</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Chinese Government Scholarship (CSC) – bilateral</td><td>Bachelor''s (limited, e.g. Medicine), Master''s, PhD</td><td>Tuition, accommodation, monthly stipend, medical insurance</td><td>English-taught or Chinese-taught; HSK for Chinese-taught; CSCA increasingly needed for bachelor''s</td><td>Typically November–January for the following September</td><td>Ministry of Education notice and portal; Chinese Embassy in Colombo</td></tr><tr><td>Chinese Government Scholarship – university programme</td><td>Mainly Master''s and PhD</td><td>Same as above when full</td><td>As per university</td><td>Typically December–April</td><td>Directly to the Chinese university, then the CSC online system</td></tr><tr><td>Provincial and university scholarships (China)</td><td>Bachelor''s to PhD</td><td>Full or partial tuition waiver, sometimes housing and stipend</td><td>As per university</td><td>Typically January–June</td><td>Directly to the university</td></tr><tr><td>International Chinese Language Teachers Scholarship (Confucius Institute / CIS)</td><td>Chinese language: one semester, one year; MTCSOL master''s</td><td>Tuition, accommodation, stipend, insurance</td><td>HSK and HSKK scores (level depends on programme)</td><td>Typically by 15 May for September; by 31 October for March</td><td>Online at chinese.cn, usually with a Confucius Institute recommendation</td></tr><tr><td>Japan MEXT</td><td>Undergraduate; research students (postgraduate)</td><td>Tuition, monthly allowance (JPY 117,000 for 2027 undergraduates), return airfare, 1-year Japanese course</td><td>Good English; written test includes Japanese</td><td>Undergraduate: typically April–May</td><td>Ministry of Education portal, then embassy test and interview</td></tr><tr><td>Korea GKS (embassy track)</td><td>Master''s, PhD (undergraduate places rare)</td><td>Fully funded, including 1 year of Korean language study</td><td>Per GKS guidelines (TOPIK or English scores add points)</td><td>Graduate: typically February–March</td><td>Paper application to the Korean Embassy, Colombo</td></tr><tr><td>Commonwealth Scholarships (UK)</td><td>Master''s, PhD</td><td>Tuition, living allowance, flights</td><td>Must meet UK university requirement</td><td>Typically September–mid October</td><td>CSC UK online system plus Ministry of Education nomination (9 master''s, 6 PhD nominations in 2025)</td></tr><tr><td>Chevening (UK)</td><td>One-year Master''s</td><td>Tuition, monthly stipend, travel, allowances</td><td>Must meet UK university requirement</td><td>Typically August–early October (2027–28 cycle closed 6 Oct 2026)</td><td>Directly at chevening.org; 2 years'' work experience</td></tr><tr><td>Australia Awards</td><td>Master''s only (for Sri Lanka)</td><td>Fully funded</td><td>IELTS or equivalent per Australia Awards rules</td><td>Typically February–April (2027 intake closed 30 Apr 2026)</td><td>Directly online; must return home for 2 years</td></tr><tr><td>DAAD EPOS (Germany)</td><td>Master''s, some PhD</td><td>Monthly stipend, insurance, travel</td><td>English or German per course</td><td>Varies by course (often August–October)</td><td>Directly to the participating German course; Sri Lanka is on DAAD''s eligible country list; 2 years'' work experience usually needed</td></tr><tr><td>Türkiye Burslari</td><td>Associate, bachelor''s, master''s, PhD</td><td>Tuition, monthly stipend, accommodation, health insurance, return flight</td><td>Turkish preparatory year is commonly provided</td><td>Typically 10 January–20 February</td><td>Directly at turkiyeburslari.gov.tr</td></tr><tr><td>Stipendium Hungaricum</td><td>Bachelor''s, master''s, PhD</td><td>Tuition, monthly stipend, accommodation, insurance</td><td>English-taught courses need proof of English</td><td>Typically mid-November to mid-January</td><td>Hungarian portal plus Ministry of Education nomination (2025–2027 agreement)</td></tr><tr><td>Russian Government quota</td><td>Vocational, bachelor''s, master''s, PhD</td><td>Tuition-free study place (living costs mostly your own)</td><td>Russian preparatory year usual for Russian-taught courses</td><td>Typically October–December</td><td>Online at education-in-russia.com; Russian House, Colombo</td></tr><tr><td>India ICCR (Aid to Sri Lanka Scholarship Scheme)</td><td>Bachelor''s, master''s, PhD (no medical or law)</td><td>Tuition, monthly allowance, accommodation support, books grant</td><td>English</td><td>Typically January–March</td><td>ICCR A2A portal; notices from High Commission of India and Ministry of Education</td></tr><tr><td>Pakistan Allama Iqbal Scholarships</td><td>Bachelor''s, master''s, PhD</td><td>Full tuition, accommodation and study allowances, books, one return ticket</td><td>English</td><td>Typically May–July (2026 call closed 5 July 2026)</td><td>Online through HEC Pakistan; scheme for 1,000 Sri Lankans over five years, renewal not yet announced</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Two other routes are worth knowing. The Sri Lankan government''s own overseas undergraduate scholarship, approved by Cabinet in July 2025, funds top A/L students at foreign universities ranked in the global top 500. Its first group of 32 students was selected in 2026.</p><h2>What China scholarships can Sri Lankan students get?</h2><p>Sri Lankan students can apply for four main types of China scholarship: the Chinese Government Scholarship (CSC) through the bilateral quota, the CSC university programme, provincial or city scholarships, and university scholarships. The International Chinese Language Teachers Scholarship covers Chinese-language study. China has more scholarship routes open to Sri Lankans than any other country in this guide.</p><h3>Chinese Government Scholarship (CSC)</h3><p>The Chinese Government Scholarship is administered by the China Scholarship Council. A full award covers tuition, university accommodation, a monthly stipend and comprehensive medical insurance. The widely published stipend rates are CNY 2,500 a month for undergraduates, CNY 3,000 for master''s students and CNY 3,500 for PhD students; confirm the current rate with your university, because rates are set by the Chinese government.</p><p>The bilateral quota is small. Reports of the 2025/2026 award ceremony at the Chinese Embassy put Sri Lanka''s total at 30 full scholarships, mostly for master''s and PhD study, and an earlier Ministry of Education notice offered only five undergraduate places, for Medicine. The university programme is a second, larger route: you apply to a Chinese university that holds CSC places, and the university nominates you. Read our <a href=\"/guides/chinese-government-scholarship-sri-lanka\">Chinese Government (CSC) scholarship guide</a> for eligibility, documents and step-by-step instructions.</p><h3>University and provincial scholarships</h3><p>Many Chinese universities offer their own scholarships, from a full package to a partial tuition waiver for the first year. Provincial and city governments (for example in Beijing, Shanghai and Jiangsu) also fund international students at universities in their region. These awards are less competitive than CSC and are often decided with your admission.</p><h3>Language and entrance tests: HSK and CSCA</h3><p>English-taught degrees do not need Chinese, but Chinese-taught bachelor''s degrees usually need HSK 4 or above, and scholarship applicants with an HSK certificate stand out. For undergraduate entry, many Chinese universities now use the China Scholastic Competency Assessment (CSCA). See the <a href=\"/guides/learn-chinese-hsk-sri-lanka\">HSK guide for Sri Lankan students</a> and the <a href=\"/guides/csca-exam-sri-lanka\">CSCA exam guide</a>. For timing, use the <a href=\"/guides/china-university-intakes-and-deadlines\">China university intakes and deadlines guide</a>.</p><h3>Confucius Institute (CIS) scholarship</h3><p>The International Chinese Language Teachers Scholarship funds one-semester and one-year Chinese language programmes and the Master of Chinese International Education. Applicants are usually aged 16–35. Host universities listed deadlines of 15 May 2026 for September 2026 entry and 31 October 2026 for March 2027 entry. Sri Lankan applicants can ask the Confucius Institutes at the University of Kelaniya or the University of Colombo about recommendation and HSK testing.</p><h2>What does \"fully funded\" really mean?</h2><p>A fully funded scholarship pays tuition and gives a living allowance, and usually covers accommodation, insurance and often flights. A partial scholarship pays only part, most often tuition, leaving you to fund living costs. The label \"fully funded\" is used loosely online, so read the coverage list in the official call.</p><ul><li><strong>Fully funded examples:</strong> Chevening, Commonwealth, Australia Awards, MEXT, GKS, full CSC, Türkiye Burslari, Stipendium Hungaricum.</li><li><strong>Often partial:</strong> Chinese university scholarships (tuition waiver only), Russian Government quota places (free tuition, living costs your own).</li><li><strong>Costs that are almost never covered:</strong> passport, police report, medical test, document attestation, visa fee, and the deposit or first month''s costs on arrival.</li></ul><p>Budget for those first costs even with a full award. Our <a href=\"/guides/cost-of-studying-in-china-for-sri-lankans\">cost of studying in China guide</a> lists typical living costs if a scholarship is partial.</p><h2>Undergraduate or postgraduate scholarships: which are easier to get?</h2><p>Postgraduate scholarships are far more numerous for Sri Lankans than undergraduate ones. Chevening, Commonwealth, Australia Awards, DAAD and GKS (embassy track) are master''s or PhD only, and the China bilateral quota is mostly postgraduate. A/L students have fewer but real options.</p><h3>Undergraduate scholarships for Sri Lankan students</h3><p>The main undergraduate options are Japan MEXT (Maths stream, three A/L passes, age limits apply), Türkiye Burslari, Stipendium Hungaricum, the Russian quota, India ICCR, Pakistan Allama Iqbal, a few CSC bilateral places, and Chinese university scholarships. Example: a Maths-stream student who missed the local university cut-off could apply for MEXT in April–May, Türkiye in January–February and Chinese university scholarships with a CSCA score, spreading the risk. Our <a href=\"/guides/what-to-do-after-al-sri-lanka\">options after A/L guide</a> compares these paths with local study.</p><h3>Postgraduate scholarships</h3><p>Postgraduate scholarships reward a strong degree (usually First or Second Upper), relevant work experience and a clear career plan. Chevening and DAAD EPOS both expect about two years'' work experience, and Chevening and Australia Awards require you to return to Sri Lanka for two years after the award. CSC and GKS PhD applications usually need a research proposal and, for CSC, often an acceptance or pre-admission letter from a supervisor.</p><h2>How do you build a strong scholarship application?</h2><p>A strong scholarship application has four parts: clean, attested documents; a specific study plan or personal statement; two strong references; and a language score. Selection panels compare hundreds of similar grades, so the written parts and references usually decide the result.</p><ol><li><strong>Choose programmes that fit.</strong> Match the course to your A/L stream or degree. A mismatch is the most common reason for rejection.</li><li><strong>Write a specific study plan.</strong> Say what you will study, why that university, and what you will do in Sri Lanka afterwards. Use real course names and examples from your own work, not general praise of the country.</li><li><strong>Get references from people who know your work.</strong> A lecturer, principal or employer who can give examples is better than a senior name who barely knows you. For CSC postgraduate applications, two recommendation letters from professors or associate professors are standard.</li><li><strong>Take the language test early.</strong> IELTS is accepted by most English-taught programmes; HSK is needed for Chinese-taught degrees in China. Book a test date that leaves time for a retake before the deadline.</li><li><strong>Prepare documents in advance.</strong> Certified copies of certificates and transcripts, passport, police clearance and medical forms take weeks in Sri Lanka. See the <a href=\"/guides/documents-for-studying-in-china-sri-lanka\">documents and attestation guide</a>.</li><li><strong>Keep everything consistent.</strong> Your name must match across passport, certificates and forms. Submit before the deadline; late or incomplete applications are rejected.</li></ol><h2>How can you avoid scholarship scams?</h2><p>Real government scholarships never charge an application or \"processing\" fee to an agent, and they never guarantee selection. If someone asks for money to secure a scholarship place, treat it as a scam. Check every call against the official website or the Ministry of Education notice.</p><ul><li><strong>Use official sites only:</strong> chevening.org, cscuk.fcdo.gov.uk, turkiyeburslari.gov.tr, education-in-russia.com, the Ministry of Education website and the embassy websites. Watch for lookalike domains; misspelled versions of the Russian portal have circulated.</li><li><strong>Be wary of \"guaranteed CSC\" offers.</strong> CSC selection is made by the Chinese side and the university, not by an agent.</li><li><strong>Never send your passport original</strong> to anyone except the embassy or visa centre when required.</li><li><strong>Check that the degree is recognised</strong> in Sri Lanka, especially for medicine: the Sri Lanka Medical Council and UGC publish their own guidance.</li></ul><p>Legitimate consultants can charge for advice and paperwork, but they should explain clearly what you are paying for and never promise a result.</p><h2>Scholarship calendar: when should Sri Lankan students apply?</h2><p>Most foreign scholarships for Sri Lankan students open between August and May for study starting the following September or October. The calendar below shows the typical months based on the latest cycles; confirm each date in the official notice for your year.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Month</th><th>What usually happens</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>August–October</td><td>Chevening (closes early October); Commonwealth UK (September to mid October); many DAAD EPOS courses; CIS deadline for March intake (31 October)</td></tr><tr><td>October–December</td><td>Russian Government quota; Stipendium Hungaricum opens (mid November); China CSC bilateral notices often appear; take HSK and CSCA</td></tr><tr><td>January–February</td><td>Stipendium Hungaricum closes (mid January); Türkiye Burslari (10 January–20 February); ICCR India; GKS graduate embassy track; CSC university programme applications open</td></tr><tr><td>March–April</td><td>Chinese university and provincial scholarships; Australia Awards (closed 30 April for 2027)</td></tr><tr><td>May–July</td><td>MEXT undergraduate (May); CIS deadline for September (15 May); Pakistan Allama Iqbal (June–July); CSC and university results</td></tr><tr><td>July–September</td><td>Admission letters, visa applications and departure</td></tr></tbody></table><p>For China in particular, the full timeline from scholarship application to arrival is in our <a href=\"/guides/study-in-china-from-sri-lanka\">complete guide to studying in China from Sri Lanka</a>, and the visa step is explained in the <a href=\"/guides/china-student-visa-sri-lanka\">China student visa guide</a>.</p><h2>How Proton Education Services can help</h2><p>Proton Education Services helps Sri Lankan students with China only: choosing universities, applying for CSC and university scholarships, preparing for the CSCA and HSK, and the X1/X2 visa. For other countries, apply directly using the official links below. See our <a href=\"/services/education\">study in China service</a> or <a href=\"/contact\">contact our team</a> on WhatsApp +94 74 201 6755.</p><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href=\"https://uom.lk/eap/news/japanese-government-mext-scholarships-2027-ministry-education-higher-education-and\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">University of Moratuwa – Japanese Government MEXT Scholarships 2027 (Ministry of Education notice)</a>, accessed 23 Oct 2026</li><li><a href=\"https://moe.gov.lk/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/21/chinese_web_notice.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ministry of Education Sri Lanka – Chinese Government Scholarship notice</a>, accessed 23 Oct 2026</li><li><a href=\"https://moe.gov.lk/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/21/Hungarian_web_notice.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ministry of Education Sri Lanka – Stipendium Hungaricum notice</a>, accessed 23 Oct 2026</li><li><a href=\"https://www.adaderana.lk/news/111470/30-sri-lankan-students-receive-chinese-govt-scholarships\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ada Derana – 30 Sri Lankan students receive Chinese govt scholarships</a>, accessed 23 Oct 2026</li><li><a href=\"https://www.tsinghua.edu.cn/enven/EAA/Financial_Aids.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Tsinghua University – Financial Aids (CSC stipend rates)</a>, accessed 23 Oct 2026</li><li><a href=\"https://isdplus.pku.edu.cn/info/1503/2905.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Peking University – Chinese Government Scholarship notice</a>, accessed 23 Oct 2026</li><li><a href=\"https://intlstu.sufe.edu.cn/ef/5b/c18056a257883/page.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Shanghai University of Finance and Economics – 2026 International Chinese Language Teachers Scholarship</a>, accessed 23 Oct 2026</li><li><a href=\"https://www.chevening.org/scholarship/sri-lanka/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Chevening – Sri Lanka</a>, accessed 23 Oct 2026</li><li><a href=\"https://www.sundaytimes.lk/250831/education/commonwealth-scholarships-available-for-postgraduate-studies-610433.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Sunday Times Sri Lanka – Commonwealth scholarships available for postgraduate studies</a>, accessed 23 Oct 2026</li><li><a href=\"https://www.newcastle.edu.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0008/1115855/AA2027_SriLanka_Study_Guide.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Australia Awards – 2027 Sri Lanka Study Guide</a>, accessed 23 Oct 2026</li><li><a href=\"https://events.australiaawardssouthasiamongolia.org/eligibility-check/sri-lanka\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Australia Awards South Asia and Mongolia – Sri Lanka eligibility</a>, accessed 23 Oct 2026</li><li><a href=\"https://overseas.mofa.go.kr/lk-en/brd/m_2309/view.do?seq=760077\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Embassy of the Republic of Korea in Sri Lanka – GKS Graduate (Embassy Track) notice</a>, accessed 23 Oct 2026</li><li><a href=\"https://daad.de/epos-info\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">DAAD – Development-Related Postgraduate Courses (EPOS)</a> and <a href=\"https://static.daad.de/media/daad_de/pdfs_nicht_barrierefrei/in-deutschland-studieren-forschen-lehren/dac_laenderliste_epos.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">DAAD – EPOS eligible country list</a>, accessed 23 Oct 2026</li><li><a href=\"https://www.ytb.gov.tr/en/news/turkiye-scholarships-2026-applications-are-now-open\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YTB – Türkiye Scholarships 2026 applications</a>, accessed 23 Oct 2026</li><li><a href=\"https://delhi.mfa.gov.hu/en/articles/ambassador-istvan-szabo-signed-a-memorandum-of-understanding-in-colombo-on-the-hungarian-sri-lankan-stipendium-hungaricum-scholarship-program-for-the-years-2025-2027-on-november-4-2025\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Embassy of Hungary – Stipendium Hungaricum MoU with Sri Lanka 2025–2027</a>, accessed 23 Oct 2026</li><li><a href=\"https://www.ft.lk/education/Over-100-SL-students-receive-Russian-State-scholarships/10515-798307\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Daily FT – Over 100 SL students receive Russian State scholarships</a>, accessed 23 Oct 2026</li><li><a href=\"https://www.hcicolombo.gov.in/page/india-sri-lanka-educational-relations/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">High Commission of India, Colombo – India–Sri Lanka Educational Relations</a>, accessed 23 Oct 2026</li><li><a href=\"https://www.hec.gov.pk/english/scholarshipsgrants/pshecp/aiss/Pages/default.aspx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">HEC Pakistan – Allama Iqbal Scholarships for Sri Lankan Students</a>, accessed 23 Oct 2026</li><li><a href=\"https://newsfirst.lk/2025/07/02/cabinet-greenlights-rs-200m-overseas-scholarship-program\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Newsfirst – Cabinet greenlights Rs 200m overseas scholarship program</a>, accessed 23 Oct 2026</li></ul>","faq":[{"q":"Which countries offer fully funded scholarships to Sri Lankan students?","a":"China (CSC), Japan (MEXT), Korea (GKS), the UK (Chevening and Commonwealth), Australia (Australia Awards, master''s only), Türkiye, Hungary, India (ICCR) and Pakistan (Allama Iqbal) all run government scholarships Sri Lankans can apply for. Coverage differs, so read each official call to see whether tuition, stipend, housing and flights are all included."},{"q":"Where are foreign scholarship notices for Sri Lankans published?","a":"Many government-to-government scholarships are published by the Ministry of Education, Higher Education and Vocational Education on its website, with online applications through foreignscholarships.mohe.gov.lk. Others are announced by the embassy in Colombo or on the scholarship''s own site, such as chevening.org or turkiyeburslari.gov.tr."},{"q":"Can I get a foreign scholarship straight after A/L?","a":"Yes, but there are fewer undergraduate awards than postgraduate ones. Japan MEXT, Türkiye Burslari, Stipendium Hungaricum, the Russian quota, India ICCR, Pakistan Allama Iqbal and Chinese university scholarships accept school leavers. Most need good A/L results, and some set age limits or stream requirements, such as Maths stream for MEXT."},{"q":"Do I need IELTS for scholarships abroad?","a":"Most English-taught programmes in the UK, Australia, Germany and Hungary ask for IELTS or an equivalent test. China, Korea and Japan often accept other proof of English for English-taught courses, while Chinese-taught degrees need HSK. Check the language rule in each university''s admission guide before booking a test."},{"q":"Is it easy to get the Chinese Government Scholarship from Sri Lanka?","a":"The bilateral quota is small, with about 30 full awards reported for 2025/2026, mostly postgraduate. Applying through the CSC university programme and for Chinese university or provincial scholarships at the same time improves your chances. A focused study plan, strong references and an HSK or CSCA score also help."}]}}', 3, 'A')
