IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM syst.Guide WHERE Slug = 'csca-exam-sri-lanka')
    INSERT INTO syst.Guide (Slug, CoverImageURL, Icon, Color, ContentJSON, SortOrder, IsActive)
    VALUES ('csca-exam-sri-lanka', '', 'book-open', 'purple', N'{"en":{"title":"CSCA Exam for Sri Lankan Students: What It Is, Subjects & How to Prepare (2027)","seoTitle":"CSCA Exam Sri Lanka: Subjects, Format & Prep 2027 | Proton","description":"CSCA exam Sri Lanka guide: who must sit it, which papers suit your A/L stream, format, scoring and a 1- or 3-month prep plan. Plan your 2027 application.","bodyHtml":"<p><strong>In short:</strong> the CSCA (China Scholastic Competency Assessment) is the entrance test China now uses for international bachelor''s degree applicants. For Sri Lankan students, the CSCA exam is required if you apply for an undergraduate place at a Chinese Government Scholarship university for 2026 or 2027 entry, and it is open to anyone else planning to study in China. You take Mathematics plus the subjects your programme asks for, online from Sri Lanka or at a test centre.</p>\n<p>This guide explains what the CSCA exam is, which papers a Sri Lankan A/L student should sit, how the test is scored, and how to prepare in one or three months. For the sign-up steps, see our separate <a href=\"/guides/csca-exam-registration\">CSCA registration guide</a>.</p>\n<h2>What is the CSCA exam?</h2>\n<p>The CSCA exam (来华留学本科入学学业水平测试) is a standardised academic test for international students applying to undergraduate programmes in China. It is run through the China Scholarship Council''s official CSCA website, csca.cn, and the first sitting was held on 21 December 2025. Universities read CSCA scores alongside your A/L results and other documents.</p>\n<p>Think of the CSCA as China''s version of the SAT: it checks whether you are academically ready for first-year university study, in one common format that applicants from every country sit.</p>\n<h2>Who needs to take the CSCA?</h2>\n<p>The CSCA is mandatory for international students applying to undergraduate programmes at Chinese Government Scholarship (CSC) universities for the 2026 and 2027 academic years. Shanghai''s official FAQ describes the test as open to all students planning to study in China, and university notices indicate it will later extend to all international undergraduate applicants.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>CSC scholarship applicants (bachelor''s):</strong> required. If you are applying through the <a href=\"/guides/chinese-government-scholarship-sri-lanka\">Chinese Government Scholarship</a>, plan your CSCA sitting well before the scholarship deadline.</li>\n<li><strong>Self-funded bachelor''s applicants:</strong> many universities that take CSC students now ask all undergraduate applicants for CSCA scores. Check each university''s admission notice.</li>\n<li><strong>Master''s and PhD applicants:</strong> the CSCA is an undergraduate entrance test, so it does not apply.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Two exemptions are published: applicants to fully English-taught undergraduate programmes do not need the Professional Chinese paper, and applicants to Chinese Language programmes with a valid HSK Level 4 score are exempt from Professional Chinese. Neither exemption removes Mathematics.</p>\n<h2>What subjects are in the CSCA exam?</h2>\n<p>The CSCA has four subjects: Professional Chinese (Humanities or STEM version), Mathematics, Physics and Chemistry. Mathematics is compulsory for every applicant. Applicants to science, engineering, agriculture or medicine programmes must also take at least one of Physics or Chemistry, and Chinese-taught programmes need the matching Professional Chinese paper.</p>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Paper</th><th>Questions</th><th>Time</th><th>Test language</th><th>Who takes it</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>Mathematics</td><td>48 multiple choice</td><td>60 minutes</td><td>Chinese or English</td><td>Every applicant</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Physics</td><td>48 multiple choice</td><td>60 minutes</td><td>Chinese or English</td><td>Science, engineering, agriculture, medicine (at least one of Physics/Chemistry)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Chemistry</td><td>48 multiple choice</td><td>60 minutes</td><td>Chinese or English</td><td>Science, engineering, agriculture, medicine (at least one of Physics/Chemistry)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Professional Chinese – STEM</td><td>80 multiple choice</td><td>90 minutes</td><td>Chinese</td><td>Chinese-taught science, engineering and medical programmes</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Professional Chinese – Humanities</td><td>80 multiple choice</td><td>90 minutes</td><td>Chinese</td><td>Chinese-taught humanities, social science, business and arts programmes</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Each CSCA subject is scored out of 100. The official sources do not publish a single pass mark; each university sets its own expectations, so treat your CSCA score as competitive rather than pass/fail.</p>\n<h2>Which CSCA papers should a Sri Lankan A/L student take?</h2>\n<p>Your CSCA papers depend on the degree you apply for, not your A/L stream as such, but the stream is a useful starting point. The table below is a typical guide based on the published rules; the admission notice of each target university is the final word, so check it before you register.</p>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>A/L stream</th><th>Typical degree choice</th><th>English-taught programme</th><th>Chinese-taught programme</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>Physical Science (Maths)</td><td>Engineering, computing, physics</td><td>Mathematics + Physics (often Chemistry too)</td><td>Mathematics + Physics/Chemistry + STEM Chinese</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Biological Science</td><td>Medicine (MBBS), pharmacy, agriculture, life sciences</td><td>Mathematics + Chemistry (Physics if the university asks)</td><td>Mathematics + Chemistry/Physics + STEM Chinese</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Commerce</td><td>Business, economics, management</td><td>Mathematics</td><td>Mathematics + Humanities Chinese</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Arts</td><td>Languages, law, social sciences, education</td><td>Mathematics</td><td>Mathematics + Humanities Chinese (Chinese Language programmes: HSK 4 can replace it)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Technology</td><td>Engineering technology, IT</td><td>Mathematics + Physics</td><td>Mathematics + Physics + STEM Chinese</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Commerce and Arts students should note that CSCA Mathematics is still compulsory even without Combined Maths at A/L. Biological Science students aiming at medicine should also read the <a href=\"/guides/mbbs-in-china-sri-lanka\">MBBS in China guide</a>, because medical schools set extra entry conditions.</p>\n<h2>How is the CSCA exam taken, and how often?</h2>\n<p>The CSCA is offered in three formats: a home-based online test with a live remote proctor, a computer-based test at an authorised test centre, and a paper-based test at a test centre. Sri Lankan students usually take the home-based online version, which needs a computer, a second device such as a phone for the proctor camera, and stable internet.</p>\n<p>From 2026 the CSCA runs about five times a year, with sessions timed for different regions: the December, April and June sittings fall in Asia-Pacific daytime, which suits Sri Lanka. Each subject has its own slot on exam day (Beijing time: Professional Chinese 1:00–2:30 pm, Mathematics 3:30–4:30 pm, Physics 5:30–6:30 pm, Chemistry 7:30–8:30 pm; Sri Lanka is 2.5 hours behind). Session dates change, so confirm the current list on csca.cn.</p>\n<p>CSCA results for online and computer-based tests come out within 7 working days, and paper-based results within 14 working days. You can sit a later session to improve a score; confirm with each university which attempt it will use. The fee is CNY 450 for one subject or CNY 700 for two or more subjects (as listed in the Shanghai government FAQ); check the fee on csca.cn when you register.</p>\n<h2>How should I prepare for the CSCA exam?</h2>\n<p>Start CSCA preparation from the official syllabi (exam outlines) and sample tests, which can be downloaded free from <a href=\"https://csca.cn/home\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">the official CSCA website</a>. CSCA Mathematics, Physics and Chemistry overlap heavily with Sri Lankan O/L and A/L content, so most of the work is learning the question style and the time pressure: 48 questions in 60 minutes is about 75 seconds per question.</p>\n<p>Be careful with \"CSCA past papers\" sold online. The exam only began in December 2025, so very few real papers exist; rely on the official sample and simulation tests and on well-made mock tests rather than unofficial collections.</p>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Plan</th><th>Who it suits</th><th>Focus</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>3 months (about 12 weeks)</td><td>Commerce/Arts students new to the Maths topics, anyone taking STEM or Humanities Chinese, or students some years past A/L</td><td>Weeks 1–6: theory topic by topic against the official syllabus. Weeks 7–10: timed exam-style question sets and an error log. Weeks 11–12: 2–3 full mock tests under real timing, then revise weak topics.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>1 month (about 4 weeks)</td><td>Recent Maths or Bio stream students who already know the content</td><td>Week 1: read the syllabus and find gaps. Weeks 2–3: 30–40 timed questions a day per subject. Week 4: two full mock tests, fix recurring mistakes, technical check for the online test.</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Professional Chinese is the hardest CSCA paper for most Sri Lankan students, because it tests academic Chinese for first-year university, not everyday conversation. Allow months, not weeks, and see our <a href=\"/guides/learn-chinese-hsk-sri-lanka\">HSK and learning Chinese guide</a> if you are starting from zero.</p>\n<h2>CSCA preparation courses at Proton</h2>\n<p>Proton Education Services runs online CSCA preparation courses for each subject, with exam-style questions and full mock tests. Fees as listed on the Proton website in October 2026:</p>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Course</th><th>Length</th><th>Mock exams</th><th>Fee</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>CSCA 1 month Mathematics</td><td>16 hours, online</td><td>2</td><td>LKR 25,000</td></tr>\n<tr><td>CSCA 1 month Physics</td><td>16 hours, online</td><td>2</td><td>LKR 25,000</td></tr>\n<tr><td>CSCA 1 month Chemistry</td><td>16 hours, online</td><td>2</td><td>LKR 25,000</td></tr>\n<tr><td>CSCA 3 months Mathematics</td><td>48 hours, online</td><td>3</td><td>LKR 35,000</td></tr>\n<tr><td>CSCA 3 months Physics</td><td>48 hours, online</td><td>3</td><td>LKR 35,000</td></tr>\n<tr><td>CSCA 3 months Chemistry</td><td>48 hours, online</td><td>3</td><td>LKR 35,000</td></tr>\n<tr><td>CSCA 3 months STEM Chinese</td><td>48 hours, online</td><td>–</td><td>LKR 40,000</td></tr>\n<tr><td>CSCA 3 months Humanities Chinese</td><td>48 hours, online</td><td>–</td><td>LKR 40,000</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>A free short CSCA introduction video is also available. You can book any of these courses on the <a href=\"/register\">Proton course registration page</a>.</p>\n<h2>How does the CSCA fit into my China application?</h2>\n<p>The CSCA is one step in a longer study-in-China application: choose universities and programmes, sit the CSCA, then submit admission and scholarship applications before each deadline. Because CSCA results take up to 14 working days, sit the exam early enough to retake before your earliest deadline; the <a href=\"/guides/china-university-intakes-and-deadlines\">China university intakes and deadlines guide</a> lists the 2027 dates. For the full picture, start with our <a href=\"/guides/study-in-china-from-sri-lanka\">complete guide to studying in China from Sri Lanka</a>.</p>\n<h2>How Proton Education Services can help</h2>\n<p>Proton Education Services helps Sri Lankan students choose the right CSCA papers for their target universities, prepare with subject courses and mock tests, and then handle university admission, CSC scholarship and visa applications. See our <a href=\"/services/education\">study in China service</a> or <a href=\"/contact\">contact the Proton team</a> on WhatsApp +94 74 201 6755.</p>\n<h2>Sources</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://csca.cn/home\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CSCA official website – China Scholastic Competency Assessment</a> (accessed 23 Oct 2026)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://english.shanghai.gov.cn/en-FAQs-StudyinShanghai/20251218/134bb78943f640519e2185ff83051f5d.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Shanghai Municipal Government – China Scholastic Competency Assessment: FAQs</a> (accessed 23 Oct 2026)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.uni-marburg.de/de/international/profil/china-kompetenz-marburg/veranstaltungen/nachrichten/china-introduces-new-global-academic-assessment\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">University of Marburg – China introduces new global academic assessment</a> (accessed 23 Oct 2026)</li>\n<li>Proton Education Services – CSCA course list, protonbusiness.com (accessed 23 Oct 2026)</li>\n</ul>","faq":[{"q":"Is the CSCA exam compulsory for Sri Lankan students?","a":"The CSCA is compulsory if you apply for a bachelor''s programme at a Chinese Government Scholarship university for 2026 or 2027 entry, which covers CSC scholarship applicants. Many universities also ask self-funded undergraduate applicants for CSCA scores, so read each university''s admission notice. Master''s and PhD applicants do not take the CSCA."},{"q":"Can I take the CSCA exam in English?","a":"Yes for the science subjects. Mathematics, Physics and Chemistry can each be taken in English or Chinese, so students applying to English-taught programmes normally choose English. Professional Chinese is a Chinese-language paper by design, and students on fully English-taught programmes are exempt from it."},{"q":"Can I sit the CSCA from Sri Lanka?","a":"Yes. The CSCA offers a home-based online test with a live remote proctor, so you can sit it at home in Sri Lanka with a computer, a phone as a second camera and stable internet. Computer-based and paper-based versions run at authorised test centres; check csca.cn for current locations."},{"q":"What is a good CSCA score?","a":"Each CSCA subject is marked out of 100, and there is no single official pass mark. Each university decides how it weighs the score alongside your A/L results, and competitive universities and scholarship places expect higher marks. Put most effort into Mathematics, which every applicant sits."},{"q":"Where can I find CSCA past papers and mock tests?","a":"Because the first CSCA sitting was in December 2025, genuine past papers are scarce. Use the free official exam outlines, sample materials and simulation tests on csca.cn first, then add timed mock tests from a structured preparation course to practise the 48-question, 60-minute format."},{"q":"How much does the CSCA exam cost?","a":"The Shanghai government FAQ lists CNY 450 for one subject and CNY 700 for two or more subjects, paid online by card when you register on csca.cn. Fees can change between sessions, so confirm the amount on the official site when you register."}]}}', 4, 'A')
GO

UPDATE syst.Guide SET ContentJSON = JSON_MODIFY(ContentJSON, '$.en', JSON_QUERY(N'{"title":"CSCA Exam Registration: How to Register for the CSCA Exam from Sri Lanka","seoTitle":"CSCA Exam Registration: Step-by-Step Guide | Proton","description":"CSCA exam registration step by step: account, sessions, online or centre format, CNY 450/700 fees and paying from Sri Lanka. Plan your next window now.","bodyHtml":"<p><strong>In short:</strong> CSCA exam registration is done only online at <a href=\"https://csca.cn/home\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">csca.cn</a>, the official China Scholastic Competency Assessment site. You create an account, choose a test session and format (home-based online or a test centre), select your subjects, and pay CNY 450 for one subject or CNY 700 for two or more. Each registration window is short, so check the site for the next one well before your university deadline.</p><p><strong>Next registration window (checked 23 Oct 2026):</strong> the October 2026 registration window has now closed. Dates for the next sessions are published on <a href=\"https://csca.cn/home\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">csca.cn</a>, and we could not confirm them from the official site on 23 October 2026. Log in to your CSCA account, open the session list on the home page, and note the registration window for the session you want. Windows are shown in Beijing time (UTC+8), which is 2 hours 30 minutes ahead of Sri Lanka time.</p><p>This page covers registration logistics only. For what the CSCA is, who needs it, which subjects suit each A/L stream and how to prepare, read our <a href=\"/guides/csca-exam-sri-lanka\">CSCA exam guide for Sri Lankan students</a>. In brief, the CSCA is the undergraduate entrance test for international students applying to Chinese universities, first held on 21 December 2025, and it is required for Chinese Government Scholarship bachelor''s applicants for the 2026 and 2027 academic years.</p><h2>What do you need before CSCA exam registration?</h2><p>Before you start CSCA exam registration, have your passport, a digital ID photo, a card that can pay online in Chinese yuan, an email address you check daily, and your final list of subjects. Registration windows last only about a week, so prepare everything in advance.</p><ul><li><strong>Passport:</strong> register with your name exactly as it appears in your passport.</li><li><strong>Digital ID photo:</strong> recent, clear, front-facing, plain background.</li><li><strong>Payment card:</strong> a credit or debit card enabled for international online payments (see the payment section below).</li><li><strong>Email address:</strong> confirmations and score notices arrive by email.</li><li><strong>Subject list:</strong> the subjects and test language each target university requires.</li><li><strong>Test format:</strong> home-based online or a test centre (check the centre list after you log in).</li><li><strong>For home-based testing:</strong> a computer, a second device such as a smartphone for the proctor camera, and a stable internet connection.</li></ul><h2>How to register for the CSCA exam, step by step</h2><p>To register for the CSCA exam, you create an account on <a href=\"https://csca.cn/home\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">csca.cn</a>, complete your profile, pick a session and format, choose subjects and test language, pay the fee and save your confirmation. With your documents ready, the process takes about 20 minutes.</p><ol><li><strong>Go to the official website.</strong> Open <a href=\"https://csca.cn/home\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">csca.cn</a> and switch to English with the 中/EN button at the top. Use only this site; look-alike sites cannot register you.</li><li><strong>Create an account.</strong> Click Register (注册), enter your email, set a password and verify your email.</li><li><strong>Complete your profile.</strong> Enter your details exactly as in your passport and upload your ID photo.</li><li><strong>Choose a test session.</strong> On the home page, find the session and its registration window (Beijing time, UTC+8).</li><li><strong>Pick your test format.</strong> Home-based online, or a computer-based or paper-based test at an authorised test centre.</li><li><strong>Select subjects and test language.</strong> Professional Chinese (Humanities or STEM track), Mathematics, Physics and/or Chemistry; the science subjects can be taken in Chinese or English.</li><li><strong>Pay the fee.</strong> CNY 450 for one subject or CNY 700 for two or more.</li><li><strong>Save your confirmation.</strong> Download or screenshot the registration confirmation; some universities accept it while you wait for scores.</li><li><strong>Before exam day,</strong> log in again to check your exam details and any admit ticket or test instructions the site issues.</li><li><strong>After the test,</strong> log in to view and download your score report, then send it to your universities.</li></ol><h2>How much is the CSCA exam registration fee?</h2><p>The CSCA exam registration fee is CNY 450 for one subject and CNY 700 for two or more subjects, according to the Shanghai government CSCA FAQ. Most Sri Lankan science-stream applicants take Mathematics plus at least one science subject, so they pay CNY 700.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Subjects registered</th><th>Fee</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>One subject</td><td>CNY 450</td></tr><tr><td>Two or more subjects</td><td>CNY 700</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The amount in Sri Lankan rupees depends on the exchange rate your bank applies on the day, plus any foreign-transaction charge. Check the current CNY rate with your bank before paying. For wider budgeting, see the <a href=\"/guides/cost-of-studying-in-china-for-sri-lankans\">cost of studying in China for Sri Lankans</a>.</p><h2>How do you pay the CSCA fee from Sri Lanka?</h2><p>You pay the CSCA fee online by card during registration. From Sri Lanka, use a credit or debit card that your bank has enabled for international online payments, and confirm that your foreign spending limit covers CNY 700.</p><p>Many Sri Lankan cards block overseas online payments by default. Call your bank or enable the setting in your banking app a day before the window opens. If a payment fails, do not pay twice; check your CSCA account and your bank statement first, and contact CSCA support if the status is unclear.</p><h2>Can I take the CSCA exam online or offline?</h2><p>Yes, the CSCA can be taken either way. There are three formats: a home-based online test with a live online proctor, a computer-based test at an authorised test centre, and a paper-based test at a test centre. You choose the format during registration.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Format</th><th>Where</th><th>Results</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Home-based online</td><td>Your own computer, live online proctoring</td><td>Within 7 working days</td></tr><tr><td>Computer-based</td><td>Authorised test centre</td><td>Within 7 working days</td></tr><tr><td>Paper-based</td><td>Authorised test centre</td><td>Within 14 working days</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Is there a CSCA exam centre in Sri Lanka?</h3><p>The first overseas CSCA exam centres opened in Vietnam and Thailand in December 2025, with more planned. We could not confirm a CSCA exam centre in Sri Lanka as of 23 October 2026, so most Sri Lankan candidates use the home-based online format. Check the centre list on <a href=\"https://csca.cn/home\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">csca.cn</a> after logging in, as new centres are added.</p><h2>Which subjects should you select, and when are they held?</h2><p>Mathematics is compulsory for everyone. Science, engineering, agriculture and medicine applicants must also take at least one of Physics or Chemistry. Professional Chinese is needed for Chinese-taught programmes but not for fully English-taught ones. Always follow each university''s admissions guide.</p><p>Mathematics, Physics and Chemistry each have 48 multiple-choice questions in 60 minutes; Professional Chinese has 80 questions in 90 minutes. Each subject is scored out of 100. The published session times, converted to Sri Lanka time (UTC+5:30), are:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Beijing time</th><th>Sri Lanka time</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Professional Chinese</td><td>1:00–2:30 pm</td><td>10:30 am–12:00 noon</td></tr><tr><td>Mathematics</td><td>3:30–4:30 pm</td><td>1:00–2:00 pm</td></tr><tr><td>Physics</td><td>5:30–6:30 pm</td><td>3:00–4:00 pm</td></tr><tr><td>Chemistry</td><td>7:30–8:30 pm</td><td>5:00–6:00 pm</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Confirm the times for your own session in your CSCA account, as they may change. Sessions held in December, April and June are scheduled for Asia-Pacific daytime, which suits Sri Lankan candidates best.</p><h2>What are the CSCA exam dates for 2027?</h2><p>The CSCA runs about five sessions a year; the 2026 pattern was January, March, April, June and December. Check the official 2027 calendar on <a href=\"https://csca.cn/home\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">csca.cn</a>, because we could not confirm the full 2027 dates from an official source on 23 October 2026.</p><p>Plan backwards from your university deadlines. Scores take up to 14 working days, so choose a session that leaves time to sit a later one if needed. Our <a href=\"/guides/china-university-intakes-and-deadlines\">China university intakes and deadlines guide</a> lists deadlines for the 2027 intake, and the <a href=\"/guides/chinese-government-scholarship-sri-lanka\">Chinese Government Scholarship guide</a> explains where CSCA scores fit in a CSC application.</p><h2>What happens on exam day and after?</h2><p>On exam day, follow the instructions issued in your CSCA account. For the home-based test, run the camera, microphone, second-device and internet checks beforehand, sit alone in a quiet, well-lit room, and keep your passport ready for identity checks. Results appear in your account within 7 working days (14 for paper tests).</p><ul><li><strong>Log in early</strong> and convert every Beijing time to Sri Lanka time.</li><li><strong>Have a power backup</strong> (UPS or charged laptop) and mobile data as a backup in case of outages.</li><li><strong>Use the same name and passport</strong> as in your registration.</li><li><strong>Download your score report</strong> once released and upload it to each university application.</li></ul><h2>Common CSCA registration mistakes</h2><ul><li><strong>Missing the window:</strong> windows last about a week; set reminders in Sri Lanka time.</li><li><strong>Wrong subjects:</strong> a missing subject can make an application incomplete.</li><li><strong>Wrong test language:</strong> for English-taught programmes, take the science subjects in English.</li><li><strong>Name mismatch:</strong> your registration name must match your passport.</li><li><strong>Card blocked:</strong> enable international online payments before the window opens.</li></ul><p>Proton Education Services runs online <a href=\"/register\">CSCA preparation courses</a> in Mathematics, Physics, Chemistry and Professional Chinese, each ending with mock exams in the CSCA style.</p><h2>How Proton Education Services can help</h2><p>Proton helps Sri Lankan students choose universities and subjects, register for the CSCA, and prepare university and scholarship applications. See our <a href=\"/services/education\">study-in-China services</a>, read the full <a href=\"/guides/study-in-china-from-sri-lanka\">study in China from Sri Lanka guide</a>, or <a href=\"/contact\">contact our team</a> on WhatsApp +94 74 201 6755.</p><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href=\"https://csca.cn/home\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CSCA official website – registration and session list</a> (accessed 23 Oct 2026)</li><li><a href=\"https://english.shanghai.gov.cn/en-FAQs-StudyinShanghai/20251218/134bb78943f640519e2185ff83051f5d.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Shanghai Municipal Government – China Scholastic Competency Assessment: FAQs</a> (accessed 23 Oct 2026)</li></ul>","faq":[{"q":"How do I register for the CSCA exam from Sri Lanka?","a":"Register online at csca.cn. Create an account with your email, enter your details exactly as in your passport, upload an ID photo, choose a session and test format, select your subjects and pay by card. Sri Lankan candidates usually choose the home-based online format and should enable international online payments on their card before the window opens."},{"q":"How much is the CSCA exam fee?","a":"The CSCA fee is CNY 450 if you register for one subject and CNY 700 for two or more subjects. Because Mathematics is compulsory and most science applicants add Physics or Chemistry, many Sri Lankan students pay CNY 700. The rupee amount depends on your bank''s exchange rate and charges on the day you pay."},{"q":"Can I take the CSCA exam online from home?","a":"Yes. The home-based online format lets you sit the CSCA on your own computer with a live online proctor. You need a computer, a second device such as a smartphone for the proctor camera and a stable internet connection. Results for online tests are released within 7 working days of the exam."},{"q":"When is the next CSCA exam registration?","a":"The October 2026 registration window has closed. Upcoming sessions and their registration windows are posted on csca.cn in Beijing time, which is 2.5 hours ahead of Sri Lanka. Check the site regularly and register as soon as the window for your chosen session opens, as windows typically last only about a week."},{"q":"Can I retake the CSCA if my score is low?","a":"The CSCA runs about five sessions a year, so you can register for a later session if you want a better score. Check with each university which score it accepts and confirm the current rules on csca.cn. Leave enough time before deadlines, as paper-based results can take up to 14 working days."}]}')), SortOrder = 5, UpdatedDate = GETDATE()
WHERE Slug = 'csca-exam-registration'
GO

IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM syst.Guide WHERE Slug = 'china-university-intakes-and-deadlines')
    INSERT INTO syst.Guide (Slug, CoverImageURL, Icon, Color, ContentJSON, SortOrder, IsActive)
    VALUES ('china-university-intakes-and-deadlines', '', 'calendar', 'teal', N'{"en":{"title":"China University Intakes 2027: March & September Deadlines for Sri Lankans","seoTitle":"China University Intake 2027: Deadlines & Calendar | Proton","description":"China university intake 2027 explained for Sri Lankans: September and March deadlines, CSC, CSCA and visa dates. See the month-by-month calendar.","bodyHtml":"<p><strong>In short:</strong> for a China university intake 2027, Sri Lankan students have two choices: the main September 2027 intake, which covers almost all degree programmes and nearly every scholarship, and a smaller March 2027 (spring) intake, used mainly for Chinese-language courses and a few degree programmes. For September 2027, the real work starts in November–December 2026, because scholarship and university windows open then and many close between February and May 2027.</p><p>This calendar marks every date as either <strong>official</strong> (taken from a named official page) or <strong>typical — confirm</strong> (based on the pattern of past years). All dates were checked 23 Oct 2026. Universities publish their 2027 notices at different times, so confirm each date on the university or scholarship page before you rely on it. For the bigger picture, start with our <a href=\"/guides/study-in-china-from-sri-lanka\">complete guide to studying in China from Sri Lanka</a>.</p><h2>What is the difference between the September and March intakes in China?</h2><p>The September intake is China''s main academic intake: degree programmes start in early September, and the Chinese Government (CSC) Scholarship is built around it. The March intake is the spring semester start. It is mainly for Chinese-language (non-degree) students and a limited number of degree programmes, and it has far fewer scholarships.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>September 2027 intake (main)</th><th>March 2027 intake (spring)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Who it suits</td><td>Bachelor''s, MBBS, Master''s and PhD students; scholarship applicants</td><td>Chinese-language students; some self-funded degree and exchange students</td></tr><tr><td>Programmes offered</td><td>Almost all programmes, English- and Chinese-taught</td><td>Mostly Chinese-language courses; selected degree programmes at some universities</td></tr><tr><td>CSC scholarship</td><td>Yes, the main CSC cycle</td><td>Rarely; plan on self-funding</td></tr><tr><td>Typical application window</td><td>Nov 2026 – May/June 2027, varies by university (typical — confirm)</td><td>Sept – Dec 2026 (typical — confirm)</td></tr><tr><td>Classes start</td><td>Early–mid September 2027</td><td>Late February – March 2027</td></tr></tbody></table><p>A useful March-intake reference point is Shanghai International Studies University''s intensive Chinese programme, which set its spring 2026 deadline as 31 December 2025 and its autumn 2026 deadline as 30 June 2026 (official, for the 2026 cycle). A spring 2027 deadline around late December 2026 is therefore likely, but that is typical — confirm on the SISU page.</p><h2>What are the key deadlines for the September 2027 intake?</h2><p>The key deadlines for a Sri Lankan student targeting September 2027 are the CSC Type A window through Sri Lanka''s Ministry of Education (typically November–January), CSC Type B and university scholarship windows (roughly November 2026 to March 2027), self-funded deadlines that can run to May 2027, and a CSCA exam sitting before you submit an undergraduate application.</p><h3>How the scholarship routes differ</h3><ul><li><strong>CSC Type A (bilateral):</strong> you apply through Sri Lanka''s Ministry of Education foreign scholarships portal (<a href=\"https://foreignscholarships.mohe.gov.lk\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">foreignscholarships.mohe.gov.lk</a>), which nominates candidates to China. The 2023 notice closed on 15 December; the window usually falls between November and January (typical — confirm when the 2027 notice is published).</li><li><strong>CSC Type B (university programme):</strong> you apply to a university that holds a CSC quota. Huazhong University of Science and Technology accepted Type B applications from 15 October 2025 to 1 March 2026 for the 2026 intake (official, 2026 cycle). Expect a similar window for 2027 (typical — confirm).</li><li><strong>University and provincial scholarships, and self-funded places:</strong> separate deadlines at each university, often later than CSC.</li></ul><p>Our <a href=\"/guides/chinese-government-scholarship-sri-lanka\">Chinese Government Scholarship guide for Sri Lankans</a> explains Type A and Type B in full.</p><h3>Named university deadlines (most recent published cycle)</h3><table><thead><tr><th>University</th><th>Route</th><th>Window (2026 intake)</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Huazhong University of Science and Technology (Wuhan)</td><td>CSC Type B</td><td>15 Oct 2025 – 1 Mar 2026</td><td>Official (2026 cycle)</td></tr><tr><td>Tongji University, College of Civil Engineering (Shanghai)</td><td>Undergraduate, Shanghai Government / Tongji scholarships</td><td>10 Jan – 31 Mar 2026</td><td>Official (2026 cycle)</td></tr><tr><td>Tongji University, College of Civil Engineering</td><td>Undergraduate, self-funded</td><td>10 Jan – 15 May 2026 (extended from 30 Apr)</td><td>Official (2026 cycle)</td></tr><tr><td>Zhejiang University, ZJU-UoE Institute</td><td>Undergraduate BSc programmes</td><td>Opens November, closes 31 May 2026</td><td>Official (2026 cycle)</td></tr></tbody></table><p>These are 2026 dates. Universities usually keep a similar pattern year to year, but they move dates, add rounds and extend deadlines, so treat the 2027 equivalents as typical — confirm. Popular programmes and scholarship quotas fill early, so aim to apply in the first round.</p><h2>Month-by-month calendar for September 2027 (November 2026 to September 2027)</h2><p>This month-by-month calendar shows what a Sri Lankan student aiming for a September 2027 start in China should do each month. Work backwards from the earliest deadline on your shortlist; if you are applying for the CSC Type A scholarship, November and December 2026 are already critical.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Month</th><th>What to do</th><th>Date status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Nov 2026</td><td>Shortlist universities and programmes. Start documents: certified O/L and A/L results, passport, police clearance, medical form. Watch the Sri Lanka MOE portal for the CSC Type A notice. Many university portals open.</td><td>Typical — confirm</td></tr><tr><td>Dec 2026</td><td>CSC Type A applications usually close (the 2023 notice closed 15 Dec). CSCA session in December. Kelaniya Confucius Institute HSK expected 13 Dec 2026.</td><td>Type A: typical — confirm. CSCA month: official. HSK: official (expected date)</td></tr><tr><td>Jan 2027</td><td>CSCA session (January). University and Type B applications in full swing; Tongji''s scholarship window opened 10 Jan in 2026.</td><td>CSCA month: official. University dates: typical — confirm</td></tr><tr><td>Feb 2027</td><td>Submit CSC Type B and early-round university applications. Many first-round scholarship deadlines fall from late February to early March.</td><td>Typical — confirm</td></tr><tr><td>Mar 2027</td><td>CSCA session (March). Type B windows close at many universities (HUST closed 1 Mar in 2026). University scholarship deadlines (Tongji: 31 Mar in 2026).</td><td>CSCA month: official. Others: typical — confirm</td></tr><tr><td>Apr 2027</td><td>CSCA session (April), often the last practical sitting for September applications. Interviews and online tests at some universities.</td><td>CSCA month: official. Others: typical — confirm</td></tr><tr><td>May 2027</td><td>Self-funded deadlines close at many universities (Tongji 15 May and ZJU-UoE Institute 31 May in 2026).</td><td>Typical — confirm</td></tr><tr><td>Jun 2027</td><td>CSCA session (June). Scholarship and admission results announced. Accept your offer and pay any deposit.</td><td>CSCA month: official. Results: typical — confirm</td></tr><tr><td>Jun–Jul 2027</td><td>Admission letter and JW201/JW202 visa form arrive by courier.</td><td>Typical — confirm</td></tr><tr><td>Jul–Aug 2027</td><td>Apply for the X1 visa at the Chinese Embassy in Colombo (processing is usually a few working days). Book flights and accommodation.</td><td>Typical — confirm</td></tr><tr><td>Late Aug – Sept 2027</td><td>Fly to China, register on the university''s stated dates, complete the medical check and apply for the residence permit within 30 days of arrival.</td><td>Registration dates: set by each university</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>CSCA sessions: what is confirmed</h3><p>The CSCA (China Scholastic Competency Assessment) runs five sessions a year from 2026, in January, March, April, June and December, according to the Shanghai Government''s CSCA FAQ (official months). December, April and June sittings are scheduled for Asia-Pacific daytime hours, which suits Sri Lanka. Exact 2027 days had not been published when we checked; confirm them on the official CSCA site. The same FAQ says the CSCA is required for undergraduate applicants to Chinese Government Scholarship universities for the 2026 and 2027 academic years, with fees of CNY 450 for one subject and CNY 700 for two or more. See our <a href=\"/guides/csca-exam-sri-lanka\">CSCA exam guide for Sri Lankans</a> and <a href=\"/guides/csca-exam-registration\">how to register for the CSCA</a>.</p><h3>HSK dates in Sri Lanka</h3><p>The Confucius Institute at the University of Kelaniya lists expected HSK sessions on 23 August, 17 October and 13 December 2026. 2027 dates were not yet published; 2026 sittings were also held in January and June, so a similar pattern is likely (typical — confirm). If your programme is Chinese-taught, book an HSK sitting at least two months before your application deadline so results arrive in time. Our <a href=\"/guides/learn-chinese-hsk-sri-lanka\">HSK guide for Sri Lanka</a> covers levels and preparation.</p><h3>Document lead times</h3><p>Documents are the most common cause of missed deadlines. Allow roughly four to eight weeks (typical — confirm) for certified results and translations, a police clearance report, attestation and the Foreigner Physical Examination Form. The <a href=\"/guides/documents-for-studying-in-china-sri-lanka\">documents guide for studying in China</a> lists each item and where to get it in Sri Lanka.</p><h2>What is the timeline for the March 2027 intake?</h2><p>The March 2027 timeline is short: apply between September and December 2026, receive the admission letter and JW202 in January 2027, and get the visa and fly in February. Because the March intake is mostly self-funded Chinese-language study, there is usually no CSC step.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Month</th><th>What to do</th><th>Date status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Sept–Nov 2026</td><td>Choose a language or spring-start programme; prepare passport, results, police report and medical form.</td><td>Typical — confirm</td></tr><tr><td>Dec 2026</td><td>Applications close at many universities (SISU''s spring 2026 deadline was 31 Dec 2025).</td><td>Typical — confirm</td></tr><tr><td>Jan 2027</td><td>Admission letter and JW202 arrive; pay fees if required.</td><td>Typical — confirm</td></tr><tr><td>Feb 2027</td><td>Apply for the visa in Colombo, fly to China, register late February – early March.</td><td>Typical — confirm</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>When does the China student visa paperwork arrive?</h2><p>For September entry, the university normally posts the admission letter and JW201 or JW202 form in June or July (typical — confirm). You then apply for an X1 (study over 180 days) or X2 visa at the Chinese Embassy in Colombo, where processing usually takes about four working days. Apply as soon as the documents arrive. Full steps are in our <a href=\"/guides/china-student-visa-sri-lanka\">China student visa guide for Sri Lankans</a>.</p><h2>What should you do if you missed a China university deadline?</h2><p>Missing one deadline rarely ends a September 2027 plan. Chinese universities stagger their windows, and self-funded deadlines run months later than scholarship ones.</p><ol><li><strong>Check for later rounds and extensions.</strong> Tongji''s College of Civil Engineering extended its 2026 self-funded undergraduate deadline from 30 April to 15 May; extensions like this are common.</li><li><strong>Switch route.</strong> If CSC Type A has closed, apply for Type B or a university or provincial scholarship at another university.</li><li><strong>Apply self-funded.</strong> Self-funded windows often stay open until May or June. Check the <a href=\"/guides/cost-of-studying-in-china-for-sri-lankans\">cost of studying in China</a> first.</li><li><strong>Use the March intake.</strong> Start a Chinese-language semester in March 2027, build your HSK level, then join a degree in September.</li><li><strong>Defer to September 2028</strong> if your target programme only takes CSC students, and use the year to raise your CSCA and HSK scores.</li></ol><h2>How Proton Education Services can help</h2><p>Proton Education Services has offices in Sri Lanka and Qingdao and helps with university selection, CSC and university scholarship applications, CSCA preparation courses and X1/X2 visa support, so each deadline above is tracked for you. See <a href=\"/services/education\">our study-in-China service</a> or <a href=\"/contact\">contact Proton</a> to plan your September or March 2027 timeline.</p><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href=\"https://english.shanghai.gov.cn/en-FAQs-StudyinShanghai/20251218/134bb78943f640519e2185ff83051f5d.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Shanghai Municipal People''s Government, China Scholastic Competency Assessment: FAQs</a>, accessed 23 Oct 2026</li><li><a href=\"https://iso.hust.edu.cn/Scholarships/FAQ.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Huazhong University of Science and Technology, Scholarships FAQ</a>, accessed 23 Oct 2026</li><li><a href=\"https://civileng.tongji.edu.cn/civilengen/Admissions/list.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Tongji University College of Civil Engineering, 2026 Admission and Scholarship Applications</a>, accessed 23 Oct 2026</li><li><a href=\"https://zje.zju.edu.cn/zje/Howtoapply/list.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Zhejiang University ZJU-UoE Institute, How to Apply</a>, accessed 23 Oct 2026</li><li><a href=\"https://www.oisa.shisu.edu.cn/index.php/en/index/lxxm/cid/136.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Shanghai International Studies University, 2026 Intensive Chinese Language Program</a>, accessed 23 Oct 2026</li><li><a href=\"https://units.kln.ac.lk/ci/index.php/cn/219-hsk-test-calendar-notice-second-half-of-2026\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Confucius Institute at the University of Kelaniya, HSK Test Calendar Notice (second half of 2026)</a>, accessed 23 Oct 2026</li><li><a href=\"https://foreignscholarships.mohe.gov.lk\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Sri Lanka Ministry of Education, Foreign Scholarships portal</a>, accessed 23 Oct 2026</li></ul>","faq":[{"q":"When is the main university intake in China for 2027?","a":"The main intake is September 2027, when nearly all bachelor''s, MBBS, master''s and PhD programmes begin and the Chinese Government Scholarship cycle runs. Applications typically open from November 2026 and close between February and May 2027 depending on the university and funding route, so Sri Lankan students should start preparing documents by November 2026."},{"q":"What is the CSC scholarship 2027 deadline for Sri Lankan students?","a":"There are two routes with different deadlines. CSC Type A goes through the Sri Lanka Ministry of Education portal, which usually closes between November and January (the 2023 notice closed on 15 December). CSC Type B goes directly to universities, often closing between late February and April 2027. Confirm each date on the official notice before applying."},{"q":"Can I start university in China in March 2027?","a":"Yes, but options are limited. The March (spring) intake is mainly for Chinese-language courses, plus a few self-funded degree programmes at some universities. Scholarships are rare. Applications usually close around December 2026, so a March start suits students who want to build their HSK level before a September degree."},{"q":"Do I need the CSCA exam for a September 2027 undergraduate application?","a":"If you are applying for an undergraduate programme at a Chinese Government Scholarship university, the Shanghai Government CSCA FAQ says the CSCA is required for the 2026 and 2027 academic years. Sessions run in January, March, April, June and December, so book a sitting that gives results before your application deadline."},{"q":"When will I get my JW202 form and visa for the September intake?","a":"Universities usually courier the admission letter and JW201 or JW202 form in June or July. With these, you apply for an X1 study visa at the Chinese Embassy in Colombo, where processing usually takes about four working days, which leaves time to fly out in late August."}]}}', 6, 'A')
